WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.642
Welcome to Module 4. We are moving from individual values to collections.

00:00:05.642 --> 00:00:12.712
Lists and tuples let Python organize several related observations so we can access, change, loop through,

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:19.292
and summarize them. A tuple is ordered like a list but is intended to stay fixed.

00:00:19.292 --> 00:00:23.797
It works well for compact records whose positions should not change.

00:00:23.797 --> 00:00:26.942
Before clicking Run, predict the output.

00:00:26.942 --> 00:00:33.087
Then run the cell, inspect the result, and change one value or condition at a time.

00:00:33.087 --> 00:00:36.432
Rerun it and explain why the output changed.

00:00:36.432 --> 00:00:41.444
The goal is to understand the relationship between input, process, and output.
